{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792268561,"nonce":"hoh+f2IwnW8ETdlCtDA+28NAchY=","message":"Correction: the title and body are wrong. Typed characters do reach the find field. The original report came from synthetic mouse and keyboard input that was mixed with the user's own input on their desktop, and could not be trusted.\n\nReproduced in-process (tests/code_find_field.rs: Cmd+F through the editor's handler, click on the field through an EventRouter, broadcast characters as the runner does): the field gets the text. What never happened is the search. The query was only read from the field inside the editor's own refresh callback, which the editor runs on events such as a hover transition, so the search ran when the pointer next crossed the editor, not as the user typed. The bar's controls (next, previous, toggles, replace) changed the data and repainted only the bar, never the editor, and the field had no on_change or Enter handling. The editor's data held no handle to refresh itself.","files":null}]}